## Home screen and bottom bar

Choose what the home screen shows, and in what order, with the Customise home button (the sliders) at
the top of Home. Settings › Customise navigation decides which pages sit in the bottom bar; the rest are
under More.

## Music during a workout

In the Android app, a music bar at the bottom of the workout screen shows what's playing in Spotify, YouTube Music or
any other music app, with play, pause and skip. Tap it for the full controls and your workout playlists.
The first time, LogIt asks you to switch it on in Android's Notification access. LogIt only uses that
access to see and control what's playing; it doesn't read your notifications, and no Spotify or Google
sign-in is needed.

Settings › Session › Music has the rest: paste a playlist's share link to save it, link a playlist to a
day of your split, start that playlist when a workout starts, and pause the music when you finish. The
music bar isn't on iPhone or the web.

## Walkthroughs

Settings › Walkthroughs has short tours of each part of the app. You can replay any of them. If you have
Pro or Studio, the full walkthroughs are on the web dashboard under Guide, and the chapters you finish
are ticked on both.

